---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const works = await getCollection('works');
const brittleThorn = works.find(work => work.id.endsWith('brittle-thorn.md'));
const { data } = brittleThorn!;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const imageLookup = new Map();
data.images?.forEach(image => imageLookup.set(image.src.split('/').pop(), image));
const imageAlt = (filename: string, fallback: string) =>
  imageLookup.get(filename)?.altText || fallback;
---

<Layout
  title="徒花棘 — The Brittle Thorn — Works"
  description={data.description}
  ogImage={data.coverImage}
>
  <JsonLd slot="head" data={data} />

  <main class="thorn-page">
    <a href={`${base}/works`} class="back-link">← Works</a>

    <header class="thorn-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-kicker">Hydon BAI / 2025</p>
        <h1>徒花棘</h1>
        <p class="hero-title-en">The Brittle Thorn</p>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Pomegranate, Pistols, and the Fragile Everyday</p>
        <blockquote>
          <span>所有易得的美丽，</span>
          <span>都长满了看不见的棘刺。</span>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="hero-quote-en">All beauty easily obtained is lined with unseen thorns.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="hero-art">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/works/brittle-thorn/anarchy-in-the-domestic.jpg`}
          alt={imageAlt('anarchy-in-the-domestic.jpg', 'Anarchy in the Domestic')}
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>Anarchy in the Domestic, 2025</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <div class="editorial-download">
      <a
        href={`${base}/downloads/hydon-bai-the-brittle-thorn-editorial-feature.pdf`}
        class="editorial-download-link"
        download
      >
        <span>Download Editorial Feature</span>
        <span>下载艺术期刊 PDF</span>
      </a>
      <div class="editorial-download-meta">
        <span>18 pages</span>
        <span>The Brittle Thorn / Hydon BAI / 2025</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="series-index" aria-label="Series themes">
      <span>Vanitas / 虚空派</span>
      <span>Domestic Order / 日常秩序</span>
      <span>Fragility / 脆弱</span>
      <span>Power / 权力</span>
    </div>

    <section class="preface">
      <div class="section-label">
        <span>Exhibition Preface</span>
        <span>展览前言</span>
      </div>

      <div class="preface-grid">
        <div class="preface-cn">
          <p class="lead">“徒花”只开花，不结果。它拥有盛放的外观，却没有通向未来的果实。</p>
          <p>在 Hydon BAI 的《徒花棘》中，餐桌看似丰盛：石榴被切开，花枝舒展，瓷盘与玻璃器皿承接着柔和的光。但这份丰盛的因果已经被倒置。枪支并非从外部闯入的异物，它安静地躺在果实中央，像一道早已被日常接纳的规则。</p>
          <p>Vanitas/虚空派以成熟的果实、盛开的花与逐渐腐败的物质提醒人们时间和生命的消逝。这个系列继承了静物画的观看方式，却改变了危险的来源：威胁不再来自未来的衰败，而来自已经潜入当下的权力。石榴汁与血迹在画面中彼此难辨，诱惑与献祭因此共享同一种颜色。</p>
          <p>上世纪七十年代，朋克以噪音、安全别针和直接的冒犯刺破体面的外壳。半个世纪后，暴力不再需要以粗粝的面貌出现。它可以变得优雅、光滑、具有设计感，进入我们的审美、消费和私人生活，并在不被察觉的情况下成为环境的一部分。</p>
          <p>《徒花棘》描绘的不是美与暴力的简单对立，而是二者如何彼此借力：美使危险变得可接受，危险又让美显得更加脆弱。我们沉浸在被赠予的丰裕之中，却逐渐失去辨认代价的能力。从甜美的接纳，到空间的失守，再到意志的自动跟从，四件作品共同构成一场发生在古典光影里的静默暴动。</p>
        </div>

        <div class="preface-en">
          <p class="lead">An adabana is a flower that blooms without bearing fruit: an appearance of fulfilment with no future growing from it.</p>
          <p>In Hydon BAI’s <em>The Brittle Thorn</em>, the table appears abundant. Pomegranates have been opened, flowers unfold, and porcelain and glass vessels receive a gentle light. Yet the logic of abundance has been reversed. The pistol is not an intruder arriving from outside. It rests quietly among the fruit, like a rule already absorbed into everyday life.</p>
          <p>Vanitas painting used ripe fruit, flowers, and decaying matter to make time and mortality visible. This series inherits the still life’s mode of looking while relocating the source of danger. The threat no longer belongs to future decay; it is a form of power already installed in the present. Pomegranate juice and blood become visually inseparable, allowing temptation and sacrifice to occupy the same colour.</p>
          <p>In the 1970s, punk tore at respectable surfaces through noise, safety pins, and direct offence. Half a century later, coercion no longer needs a brutal appearance. It can be elegant, polished, and carefully designed. It enters taste, consumption, and private space until it becomes part of the environment itself.</p>
          <p><em>The Brittle Thorn</em> is not a simple opposition between beauty and violence. It asks how the two sustain one another: beauty makes danger acceptable, while danger makes beauty appear more fragile. Across four paintings, sweetness becomes intrusion, intrusion cools into aftermath, and visible force gives way to automatic obedience—a silent riot staged in classical light.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="thorn-rule"></div>

    <section class="chapter chapter-square">
      <div class="chapter-marker">
        <span class="chapter-no">01</span>
        <span class="chapter-cn">诱惑</span>
        <span class="chapter-en">Seduction</span>
      </div>

      <div class="chapter-layout">
        <figure class="work-image work-image-square">
          <img
            src={`${base}/images/works/brittle-thorn/pretty-vacant.jpg`}
            alt={imageAlt('pretty-vacant.jpg', 'Pretty Vacant')}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>

        <div class="work-copy">
          <h2>Pretty Vacant <span>漂亮的空虚</span></h2>
          <p class="work-meta">2025 / Oil on canvas / 40 × 40 cm</p>
          <div class="work-cn">
            <p>俯视的视角把餐盘变成一座小型祭坛。切开的石榴像宝石，也像刚刚暴露的伤口；枪则被端正在盘中，成为这场宴席真正的主菜。</p>
            <p>危险没有破坏画面的精致，反而被精致包裹。我们所面对的不是强迫，而是一种甜美的交换：为了即时的满足与安全感，个体主动交出警觉，并把空虚误认为丰盛。</p>
          </div>
          <p class="work-en">Seen from above, the plate becomes a small altar. The gun does not rupture the elegance of the scene; elegance receives and presents it. Immediate pleasure becomes a soft exchange in which vigilance is surrendered and vacancy is mistaken for abundance.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter chapter-portrait">
      <div class="chapter-marker">
        <span class="chapter-no">02</span>
        <span class="chapter-cn">潜入</span>
        <span class="chapter-en">Intrusion</span>
      </div>

      <div class="chapter-layout">
        <figure class="work-image work-image-portrait">
          <img
            src={`${base}/images/works/brittle-thorn/anarchy-in-the-domestic.jpg`}
            alt={imageAlt('anarchy-in-the-domestic.jpg', 'Anarchy in the Domestic')}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>

        <div class="work-copy">
          <h2>Anarchy in the Domestic <span>日常的刺杀</span></h2>
          <p class="work-meta">2025 / Oil on canvas / 40 × 60 cm</p>
          <div class="work-cn">
            <p>水绿色桌布、花枝和玻璃器皿仍维持着夏日午后的安静，枪口却从画面下方斜向切入。石榴汁在柔和的光线中溅开，甜味与铁锈味仿佛同时抵达。</p>
            <p>家庭与餐桌原本被理解为庇护之所。作品让权力以最安静的方式进入这片私人领地：它不摧毁日常，而是寄居其中。美丽之所以脆弱，正因为它习惯于毫无防备。</p>
          </div>
          <p class="work-en">The pale tablecloth and flowering branches preserve the calm of a summer afternoon while a pistol cuts diagonally into the scene. Power does not destroy the domestic space; it inhabits it. Beauty becomes vulnerable precisely because it has learned to remain undefended.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter chapter-landscape">
      <div class="chapter-marker">
        <span class="chapter-no">03</span>
        <span class="chapter-cn">余波</span>
        <span class="chapter-en">Aftermath</span>
      </div>

      <figure class="work-image work-image-wide">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/works/brittle-thorn/the-sabotage.jpg`}
          alt={imageAlt('the-sabotage.jpg', 'The Sabotage')}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>

      <div class="work-copy work-copy-wide">
        <div>
          <h2>The Sabotage <span>静物即破坏</span></h2>
          <p class="work-meta">2025 / Oil on canvas / 40 × 60 cm</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-cn">
          <p>宴席已经退场。果汁停止流动，颜色由鲜红转向暗沉；空盘、散落的果实与冷却的花枝留在原处，枪像一个完成任务后仍未离席的见证者。</p>
          <p>五十年前的反叛制造噪音，这里的反叛却表现为冷凝。古典静物的秩序没有被高声推翻，而是在一片近乎优雅的寂静中失效。真正长久的不是盛放，而是盛放之后无法抹去的痕迹。</p>
        </div>
        <p class="work-en">The banquet has receded. Juice darkens, the plate is empty, and the gun remains like a witness that has completed its task. Rebellion appears here not as noise but as cooling matter: the quiet failure of a classical still-life order and the persistence of what cannot be undone.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter chapter-landscape chapter-final">
      <div class="chapter-marker">
        <span class="chapter-no">04</span>
        <span class="chapter-cn">驯化</span>
        <span class="chapter-en">Conditioning</span>
      </div>

      <figure class="work-image work-image-wide">
        <img
          src={`${base}/images/works/brittle-thorn/no-future.jpg`}
          alt={imageAlt('no-future.jpg', 'No Future')}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>

      <div class="work-copy work-copy-wide">
        <div>
          <h2>No Future <span>被人塑造的未来</span></h2>
          <p class="work-meta">2025 / Oil on canvas / 40 × 60 cm</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-cn">
          <p>视线降到冰冷的瓷砖地面。一只明黄色的人造小鸭紧跟象牙白高跟鞋，越过断裂的石榴、散落的花瓣和横在前方的绳索。它看似快乐，也看似没有选择。</p>
          <p>小鸭的“跟从”把系列从可见的武器带向更隐蔽的控制：最彻底的征服并不依赖强迫，而是预先塑造欲望、审美与前进的方向。当未来由他人设定，“No Future”便不再是拒绝未来，而是发现那个未来从未真正属于自己。</p>
        </div>
        <p class="work-en">A synthetic duck follows an ivory heel across broken fruit and a rope laid in its path. The series moves from visible weapons to quieter control: desire, taste, and direction shaped in advance. “No Future” becomes not a refusal of what lies ahead, but the discovery that the promised future was never one’s own.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="series-closing">
      <p>表面是甜美诱人的徒花，暗里是刺痛日常的棘刺。</p>
      <p class="closing-en">The bloom is visible. The thorn has already entered the room.</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
